vNIC DLPAR TEST
===============

Overview
--------
This test performs Dynamic Logical Partition (DLPAR) hot remove and hot
add operations on a pre-provisioned vNIC interface using the OS-level
drmgr command. It also supports running the same DLPAR cycle under
kernel lockdown (integrity or confidentiality mode).

IMPORTANT: The vNIC must already be added to the LPAR manually before
running this test. This script does NOT provision the vNIC itself.

Prerequisites
-------------
1. RSCT packages must be available in the system repository:
      ksh, src, rsct.basic, rsct.core.utils, rsct.core,
      DynamicRM, powerpc-utils
   On Ubuntu, additionally: python-paramiko
   The script will attempt to install them automatically.

2. rsct and rsct_rm services must be startable via:
      startsrc -g rsct
      startsrc -g rsct_rm

3. HMC must be reachable from the LPAR and SSH access must be available.

4. The vNIC must already exist on the LPAR (visible via lsslot and
   lshwres on HMC) before running either test case.

5. SRIOV adapter location code and port must be known (used to resolve
   the backing adapter ID from HMC).

6. For lockdown test: kernel must support
   /sys/kernel/security/lockdown (Linux 5.4+ with CONFIG_SECURITY_LOCKDOWN_LSM).

Test Cases
----------
test_vnic_dlpar
    Performs drmgr-based hot remove (-r) and hot add (-a) on each
    vNIC slot for num_of_dlpar iterations. After each cycle, verifies
    that the interface comes back up and backend traffic (ping to
    peer_ip) is restored.

test_vnic_dlpar_lockdown
    Same as test_vnic_dlpar but first enables kernel lockdown to the
    configured lockdown_mode (default: integrity). DLPAR is then
    performed under lockdown to verify the operation is not affected.
    Original lockdown state is restored in tearDown where possible.
    Note: kernel lockdown is a one-way escalation at runtime
    (none -> integrity -> confidentiality). Downgrade to 'none'
    requires a reboot.

Input Parameters
----------------
hmc_username
    HMC login username.
    Example: hscroot

hmc_pwd
    HMC login password.
    Example: abc123

manageSystem
    Managed system name as shown by: lssyscfg -r sys -F name
    Example: Server-9080-M9S-SN12345

slot_num
    Virtual slot number(s) of the vNIC interface(s).
    Space-separated for multiple vNICs.
    Valid range: 3 - 2999
    Example: "4" or "4 5"

mac_id
    MAC address(es) of the vNIC interface(s).
    Space-separated, with or without colons.
    Example: "02:03:03:03:03:01" or "02:03:03:03:03:01 02:03:03:03:03:02"

device_ip
    IP address(es) to configure on the vNIC interface(s) after DLPAR.
    Space-separated for multiple vNICs.
    Example: "192.168.1.10" or "192.168.1.10 192.168.1.11"

netmasks
    Netmask(s) corresponding to device_ip entries.
    Space-separated for multiple vNICs.
    Example: "255.255.255.0"

peer_ip
    Peer IP address(es) used for backend traffic verification (ping).
    Space-separated for multiple vNICs.
    Example: "192.168.1.20"

sriov_adapters
    Physical location code(s) of the SRIOV backing adapter(s).
    Space-separated for multiple backing devices.
    Used to resolve adapter_id from HMC lshwres output.
    Example: "U78DA.ND0.WZS0027-P0-C11"

sriov_ports
    SRIOV port number(s) corresponding to sriov_adapters.
    Space-separated.
    Example: "0" or "0 1"

num_of_dlpar
    Number of DLPAR remove/add cycles to perform per slot.
    Default: 1
    Example: 3

lockdown_enable
    Set to True to enable kernel lockdown before running DLPAR.
    Only applies to test_vnic_dlpar_lockdown.
    Default: False

lockdown_mode
    Kernel lockdown mode to activate when lockdown_enable is True.
    Accepted values: integrity, confidentiality
    Default: integrity

Example Usage
-------------
avocado run vnic_dlpar.py -m vnic_dlpar.py.data/vnic_dlpar.yaml

    Run only regular DLPAR test:
avocado run vnic_dlpar.py:VnicDlpar.test_vnic_dlpar \
    -m vnic_dlpar.py.data/vnic_dlpar.yaml

    Run only lockdown DLPAR test:
avocado run vnic_dlpar.py:VnicDlpar.test_vnic_dlpar_lockdown \
    -m vnic_dlpar.py.data/vnic_dlpar.yaml
